PPU: reservation registration is idempotent, so reused thread slots do not fill the registry.
Toro's own patch (7xxx); candidate for upstream (the bug is upstream's, still in v0.19.0).
What: ppu_resv_register takes a small lock, skips a context that is already registered, and publishes a new one
with a full barrier before the count; more distinct contexts than the 128 places stop the process with a message.
Why: thread contexts live in the fixed thread table (g_ppu_threads, 64 slots) and a finished thread's slot is reused,
so the same context was registered again at every thread start. Toro restarts one worker in slot 4 about 30 times in
its first 30 s (run tlp-pf-b: 47 starts, 12 slots), so the 128 places filled within minutes, and a slot first used
after that never had its lwarx reservation broken by other threads' stwcx (ABA on the game's lock-free lists). With
duplicates skipped the registry holds at most 65 contexts. Same fix as found in another port (thanks to its
maintainer); written here with the file's own Interlocked primitives.
--- a/runtime/ppu/ppu_loader.cpp	2026-11-09 19:19:01.431779523 -0600
+++ b/runtime/ppu/ppu_loader.cpp	2026-11-09 19:19:01.432779546 -0600
@@ -824,6 +824,12 @@
 #define PPU_RESV_INVALID 0x100000000ull   /* out of (uint32_t) ea range */
 static ppu_context* g_resv_ctxs[PPU_RESV_MAX];
 static volatile LONG g_resv_ctx_n = 0;
+/* Toro patch 7025: registration is serialized and idempotent. Thread contexts live in the fixed thread table
+ * (g_ppu_threads, PPU_THREAD_MAX 64), so a slot reused by a new thread hands the same context in again: counting
+ * every start filled the 128 places after ~127 starts (Toro restarts one worker ~30 times in its first 30 s), and a
+ * context first registered after that never had its reservation broken by other threads' stores. With duplicates
+ * skipped the list holds at most 65 contexts (64 slots + the main thread); a real overflow stops loudly. */
+static volatile LONG g_resv_reg_lock = 0;
 /* Sharded by address: a single global lock convoyed all stwcx (workers spinning
  * on a descheduled holder -> loader too slow to finish jobs). Shard by the
  * 16-byte-block of ea so unrelated structures never serialize; same-structure
@@ -840,8 +846,18 @@
 extern "C" void ppu_resv_register(ppu_context* c)
 {
     if (g_resv_store_active < 0) g_resv_store_active = getenv("PPU_RESV_STORE") ? 1 : 0;
-    long i = _InterlockedExchangeAdd(&g_resv_ctx_n, 1);
-    if (i < PPU_RESV_MAX) g_resv_ctxs[i] = c;
+    while (_InterlockedCompareExchange(&g_resv_reg_lock, 1, 0)) YieldProcessor();
+    const long n = g_resv_ctx_n;
+    for (long i = 0; i < n; i++)
+        if (g_resv_ctxs[i] == c) { _InterlockedExchange(&g_resv_reg_lock, 0); return; }
+    if (n >= PPU_RESV_MAX) {
+        fprintf(stderr, "[ppu] reservation registry full: %d distinct thread contexts\n", PPU_RESV_MAX);
+        fflush(stderr);
+        abort();
+    }
+    g_resv_ctxs[n] = c;
+    _InterlockedExchange(&g_resv_ctx_n, n + 1);   /* full barrier: the slot is written before the count shows it */
+    _InterlockedExchange(&g_resv_reg_lock, 0);
 }
 /* Where every guest thread is, as a GUEST address.
  *
